/* book Worked example: Q: An aircraft is cleared for ETOPS 120, so it must stay within 120 minutes of a suitable alternate; at 420 kt that is 840 nm. Its essential DC bus draws 2.8 kW at 28 V. The battery is rated 40 Ah and only 50 % may be used. Find the bus current, usable charge and battery time, and say what this means for the diversion.
   1. Distance = 420 kt × 2 h = 840 nm.
   2. Bus current I = P / V = 2800 W / 28 V = 100 A.
   3. Usable charge = 40 Ah × 0.50 = 20 Ah.
   4. Time t = Qusable / I = 20 Ah / 100 A = 0.2 h.
   5. 0.2 h × 60 = 12 min.
   Answer: 100 A, 20 Ah and 12 min; the RAT or APU must take over long before 120 minutes. */
