/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An LRU is a box that can be removed and replaced as one unit without opening it.
   - Civil cases follow ARINC 404, whose air transport rack (ATR) sizes run from ¼ ATR to 1 ATR, or the newer ARINC 600, whose sizes are counted in modular concept units (MCU).
   - Every watt lost as heat raises temperature.
   - Thermal resistance Rth is the temperature rise per watt, in kelvin per watt (K/W).
   - Tcase is case temperature in °C; Tair is cooling-air inlet temperature in °C; P is heat in W; Rth is case-to-air resistance in K/W.
   - Inside the box, each hot component has its own junction-to-case resistance Rjc: Tj = Tcase + Pdevice × Rjc, where Pdevice is the heat of that one component, not of the whole LRU.
   - EMI is unwanted electromagnetic energy, carried as current along a wire or as a field through space, that disturbs equipment.
   - Four controls work together.
   - RTCA DO-160 covers environmental and EMI tests; MIL-STD-461 covers military EMI.
*/
